<title>UK: NatWest in loans switch - newspaper.</title>
<headline>NatWest in loans switch - newspaper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>National Westminster Bank intends to remove $5 billion of corporate loans from its balance sheet by transforming them into securities that will be sold to international investors, The Financial Times said.</p>
<p>&quot;The deal, involving loans to 300 large companies in the U.S. and Europe, is the first of its kind in Europe,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>The plan could lead to others passing on earnings from corporate loans to investors, rather than typing up their capital to back the loans.</p>
</text>
